nvention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="EP-0483387-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>EP</country><doc-number>0483387</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-2127475-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>2127475</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit><patcit ucid="JP-5147356-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>5147356</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </patcit> </patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAYASHIBARA BIOCHEM LAB</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOHSAKA AYAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWATA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUI SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOHSAKA, AYAKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KABUSHIKI KAISHA HAYASHIBARA SEIBUTSU KAGAKU KENKYUJO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWATA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOHSAKA AYAKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWATA TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YASUI SHIGEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOHSAKA, AYAKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWATA, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YASUI, SHIGEO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic dye compound which is useful in optical recording media, contains a fluorine-containing anion as a counter ion, and has excellent solubility. The compound is an indolenine-based pentamethine cyanine dye having a specific structure. Also provided are: a light-absorbing material and an optical recording medium each containing the cyanine dye; and a process for producing the cyanine dye via the step of reacting a compound having a 3,3-dimethyl-2-(1,3-butadienyl)-3H-benzoindolenium skeleton with a compound having a 2,3,3-trimethyl-3H-benzoindolenium skeleton.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce composé colorant organique, des plus utiles pour des supports d'enregistrement optique, renferme un anion contenant du fluor comme contre-ion et sa solubilité est remarquable. Le composé est un colorant pentaméthine cyanine à base d'indolénine possédant une structure spécifique. L'invention a trait également à un matériau absorbant la lumière ainsi qu'à un support d'enregistrement optique contenant chacun le colorant cyanine. Elle porte, en outre, sur un procédé de production de ce colorant consistant à faire réagir un composé ayant un squelette 3,3-diméthyl-2-(1,3-butadiényl)-3H-benzoindolénium avec un composé ayant un squelette 2,3,3-triméthyl-3H-benzoindolénium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>